==Icelandic==
===Etymology===
From the verb ''[[leggja]]'' (meaning to "[[lay]]") + ''[[á#Icelandic|á]]'' (meaning "[[on]]") + ''[[minnið]]'' (meaning "the [[memory]]"), the {{indef}} {{acc}} {{singular}} of ''[[minni]]'' (meaning "[[memory]]"). Literally meaning to "lay on the memory".
===Noun===
'''[[leggja]] [[á#Icelandic|á]] [[minni#Icelandic|minnið]]'''

# to [[keep]] in [[mind]], to [[memorise]], to [[study]], to [[learn]]
#* ''[[allir|Allir]] [[þurfa|þurftu]] að '''leggja''' [[húsregla|húsreglurnar]] '''á minnið'''.''
#*: [[everybody|Everybody]] [[had]] to '''memorise''' the [[rules]] of the [[house]].

====Usage notes====
* The thing or object which is being ''memorised'' or ''kept in mind'', is inserted between '''[að] leggja''' and '''á minnið''', in it's [[definine]] (rarely [[indefinite]]) {{acc}} form. For example:
**''[[við|Við]] [[þurfa|þurfum]] að '''leggja''' [[allur|alla]] ({{acc}} {{singular}}) [[bók#Icelandic|bókina]] ([[definite]] {{acc}} {{singular}}) '''á minnið''' [[fyrir]] [[próf]]ið!''
**: [[we|We]] [[need]] to '''memorise''' the whole [[book]] for the [[test]].

